caption: $hgsd.new-button
title: hgsd.new-button widget
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

! Introduction
The new-button opens the new-item modal, pre-seeding it with the given parameters. The created tiddler receives the tag for `gsd-type`, and the remaining values become defaults in the modal's pickers. When placed on a tiddler (e.g. a project's view page), pass `gsd-calling-tiddler` so the creation can assign back-references and update the caller's status.

! Content and Attributes
Content becomes the button label.

|!Attribute |!Description |
|gsd-type |Item type to preselect (`action`, `project`, …) |
|gsd-status |Status to preselect (`next`, `waiting`, `future`, `active`) |
|gsd-complete |Completion value to seed (rarely used) |
|gsd-project |Project title to preselect |
|gsd-contact |Contact title to preselect |
|gsd-context |Context tag to preselect |
|gsd-realm |Realm tag name to preselect |
|gsd-update-status |`yes` lets creation also update the calling tiddler's status (used by the convert-to-project flow) |
|gsd-calling-tiddler |Title of the invoking tiddler; blank = the tiddler the button renders in. Resolves the Inheritance rules' caller harvest (realms, informal tags) and the AfterCreation rules |
|class, style, aria-label, role, tooltip, disabled |Standard button attributes |

! Panel-link stamp

When this button is rendered by a pick row (the plain "new" fallback of [[$hgsd.pick-field|hgsd.pick-field widget]] or [[$hgsd.pick-append|hgsd.pick-append widget]]), its click also stamps the row's write shape onto `$:/temp/gsd-new-state` (`hgsd-link-kind`, `hgsd-link-field`, `hgsd-link-type`), and the created item is linked to the calling tiddler exactly as the row's create-and-add would: the calling tiddler's field is set (pick-field), the created title is appended to the calling tiddler's list ("Depends on"), or the calling tiddler is appended to the created tiddler's list ("Prerequisite of"). A type switched inside the modal skips the write, and every non-pick button stamps blanks, so standalone buttons never link.

''For plugin authors'': you are unlikely to need any of this. Buttons you place yourself behave like the shipped sidebar and quick-add buttons (no link), and any pick-field/pick-append section you write links automatically, for any item type or field, with no extra wiring. The one escape hatch: a hand-rolled picker built from raw `$hgsd.pick` plus its own buttons can opt into the same linking by binding `new-kind` (`field`, `own` or `item`) and `new-link-field` in the scope around its `$hgsd.new-button`. Without them the button links nothing, exactly as before.

! Example
```
<$hgsd.new-button gsd-type="action" gsd-status="next" gsd-project=<<currentTiddler>> gsd-calling-tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>>
  new next action
</$hgsd.new-button>
```

! Relation to create-and-add

Next to this button, picker surfaces also use the shared `hgsd-create-and-add` module: when the picker's typed value names a non-existent tiddler, it offers immediate creation plus linking (`create "«typed»" and add`). This button opens the full modal instead.